   "isSolo": true,
   "levelText": "",
   "page": 0,
   "description": "<p><em>Huge monstrosity (shapechanger)</em></p><p><strong>GM:</strong> An abomination that rose through the cult's rites into a six-headed serpent. Its temple is a city, and its worshippers are its larder.</p><p><strong>Solo:</strong> acts twice a round, on its initiative and again 10 lower (the system adds its second turn; the second repeats its attacks, never a spell or limited ability). Anything that stops it acting, attacking, moving or casting ends after two of its turns (one, the second time in a fight), then nothing of the kind affects it until the end of the following round; the first time it drops to half HP every condition and hostile effect ends and its breath weapons and other limited-use abilities recover (not its spells); area, aura and ongoing damage and regeneration come once a round, at the start of its first turn (all automatic). An effect that would kill it outright, banish or imprison it, or Exhaustion from a spell, costs it its next two turns instead (yours to run); only one of Harm and Mass Harm can affect it in a fight. Damage to 0 HP still kills it.</p>",
   "treasure": "<p>Treasure type <strong>lair H</strong> (see the Treasure tables).</p>"
  }
 },
